ue" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465608} :answer-field/id #uuid "f83f0034-59a5-50e0-831e-db7daa16170b" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466647}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "82dbf453-cc10-55de-93c2-196c90ad7e6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-174329" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are false?\n- **P.** $P:$  $7$ is an odd number.\n- **Q.** $Q:$ $28$ is multiple of $7.$\n- **R.** $R:$ $|1-2|=-1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate the truth value of each statement:\n\n- Statement $P$ is *true.* Indeed, $7$ is an odd number.\n\n- Statement $Q$ is *true.* Indeed, $28$ is multiple of $7.$\n\n- Statement $R$ is *false* because $|1-2|=1\\ne -1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$R$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284707 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eda1965-d655-5550-9bb5-13e7a9c1b406" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statements Expressed Using Symbols" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049002 :topic/id #uuid "d2783ca6-3cd7-54fc-baaa-eb47c3d52ff6" :topic/math-academy-id 58 :topic/title "Statements and Predicates"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13276a8f-a2bb-5453-9295-2c3d2d2341bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465609} {:answer/id #uuid "84a1bd1d-228b-507e-9a4e-51fada7969ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84a1bd1d-228b-507e-9a4e-51fada7969ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592