 "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options:\n\n- $P$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because $2$ times  $28$ equals $56.$\n\n- $Q$ is a statement. This statement is *false* because $0.2$ is not an integer.\n\n- $R$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $Q$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284709 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eda1965-d655-5550-9bb5-13e7a9c1b406" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statements Expressed Using Symbols" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049002 :topic/id #uuid "d2783ca6-3cd7-54fc-baaa-eb47c3d52ff6" :topic/math-academy-id 58 :topic/title "Statements and Predicates"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c4ef402-8030-5d20-bbe0-b302c24558c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465621} {:answer/id #uuid "86ee4554-589b-5aa6-95dc-ba1f2e3f5542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86ee4554-589b-5aa6-95dc-ba1f2e3f5542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465622} :answer-field/id #uuid "93f36ffb-2fe7-543b-a735-116e73598ba3" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466654} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab40bcd-5ec7-55ea-9d91-bc415a6831b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465623} {:answer/id #uuid "f5ae5130-3398-5133-8e32-3d4c7e20ea2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218