 both.\n\n- $Q$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $0.5$ are equivalent forms of the same rational number.\n\n- $R$  is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $Q$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284733 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35eba041-5109-5855-b132-174c0271c168" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049002 :topic/id #uuid "d2783ca6-3cd7-54fc-baaa-eb47c3d52ff6" :topic/math-academy-id 58 :topic/title "Statements and Predicates"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a70e389-17f9-5e37-b90e-400709aef507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465627} {:answer/id #uuid "d59916c7-6624-57d3-9aa0-b89fb65593dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d59916c7-6624-57d3-9aa0-b89fb65593dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465628} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9ddd945-a9a9-5f34-9325-4506624cf8a9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466657} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e7f3fb8-bf3b-5c62-a094-0338bd342f1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465629} {:answer/id #uuid "106883a6-fb4f-554a-9d13-b593ed2e7a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e7f3fb8-bf3b-5c62-a094-0338bd342f1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465629} :answer-field/id #uuid "52dcd415-f5ef-5cb1-80ef-962e482b89de" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466658} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d5c76a5-29e5-5b34-8ef7-febafe6faa9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465631} {:answer/id #uuid "585ca251-fce3-502e-8947-1413c581d399" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d5c76a5-29e5-5b34-8ef7-febafe6faa9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465631} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8a56780-9d22-5354-9ee6-e0bbeaa0aa63" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d84a9618-171e-5da0-bc3f-857b9c134eae" :question/math-academy-id "q-175326" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n- **I.** $x$ is a negative number.\n- **II.** Why is $y$ an even number?\n- **III.** ${z}^{2}-2$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false. Rather, it will give a question.\n\n- Option III is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $z$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284735 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35eba041-5109-5855-b132-174c0271c168" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049002 :topic/id #uuid "d2783ca6-3cd7-54fc-baaa-eb47c3d52ff6" :topic/math-academy-id 58 :topic/title "Statements and Predicates"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ceb5d96-2d44-54fc-8dcc-5572d37a3103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465633} {:answer/id #uuid "288acd2a-a5b5-58e5-bf10-d8f42d8c37ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ceb5d96-2d44-54fc-8dcc-5572d37a3103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465633} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3ee974f-92e2-533f-96f0-e2967c52b8fd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466660} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "847a3ab5-6fae-5c67-ab51-d34808e1986b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465635} {:answer/id #uuid "b3dce862-dc40-5247-92ef-2f347a340762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3dce862-dc40-5247-92ef-2f347a340762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465636} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bb991ad-9e28-5b98-abdc-b8aa360c9214" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7731a299-5478-5a71-93ed-7a3f702c2404" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465637} {:answer/id #uuid "f5750c7c-8f33-5f4c-b6fb-b77c5d95cd63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5750c7c-8f33-5f4c-b6fb-b77c5d95cd63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465638} :answer-field/id #uuid "77763d58-3c99-5c78-b4d0-2499457bbaf1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466662}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "33aeb9a4-e17a-5f7f-8d45-99fe2421efca" :question/math-academy-id "q-175330" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n- **I.** The square root of $x.$\n- **II.** $y$ is a composite number.\n- **III.** $z+3$ is equal to $8.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $z$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284736 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35eba041-5109-5855-b132-174c0271c168" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049002 :topic/id #uuid "d2783ca6-3cd7-54fc-baaa-eb47c3d52ff6" :topic/math-academy-id 58 :topic/title "Statements and Predicates"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70ec8960-30b7-517b-8785-5799d6e298d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465639} {:answer/id #uuid "13333e7f-a15a-56bd-af5d-b444309eaa02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13333e7f-a15a-56bd-af5d-b444309eaa02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465640} :answer-field/id #uuid "c70ade2b-3e73-5197-a7cc-28860eba5955" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466663} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6602dd1-ddc3-510b-873c-93e37b9a2aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465641} {:answer/id #uuid "8b921c21-e96d-5055-a0dd-f68afbc05608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6602dd1-ddc3-510b-873c-93e37b9a2aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465641} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5227b23-a7e6-5cd6-b078-3c9a2c174f17" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2afb05a-0d4d-5878-9ac9-67598c55f9bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465643} {:answer/id #uuid "c7462785-9492-540d-bf47-b924f090c7d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7462785-9492-540d-bf47-b924f090c7d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465644} :answer-field/id #uuid "27e3e03c-aadc-59e3-84e4-eb2d05caddc0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466665}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a44c5510-4a7d-5483-9262-f6a148074c77" :question/math-academy-id "q-175332" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n- **I.** $z$ is an irrational number.\n- **II.** Is $x$ a positive number?\n- **III.** ${y}^{2}+1$ is prime.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $z$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option II is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false. Rather, it will give a question.\n\n- Option III is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35eba041-5109-5855-b132-174c0271c168" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049002 :topic/id #uuid "d2783ca6-3cd7-54fc-baaa-eb47c3d52ff6" :topic/math-academy-id 58 :topic/title "Statements and Predicates"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "deab7354-8d59-5651-963c-4faf3b669082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465645} {:answer/id #uuid "73d28717-f191-5e1e-95bf-5af3698729dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "deab7354-8d59-5651-963c-4faf3b669082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465645} :answer-field/id #uuid "decf0e43-3877-5a21-8037-cee318134af1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466666} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8d510c8-83d1-57f0-a77a-f71e8770f23d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 175921