9 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450100} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7fdbc26-d6af-51af-bd0e-f6efec58fa66" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451004}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "044de50e-6da8-5a08-93e7-4cbfebd23610" :question/math-academy-id "q-177658" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is a square matrix\n- **II.** $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n- **III.** $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}13 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 13\\end{bmatrix}\\ne I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A\\cdot {A}^{T}\\ne I,$ our matrix is **not** orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284753 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133948 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9017b4e-ddb3-56f6-ba30-b494a7e4e09f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Orthogonal Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049606 :topic/id #uuid "03f0df59-343c-5dd7-ad4a-b7bacf1e1f44" :topic/math-academy-id 2105 :topic/title "Orthogonal Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "838c5084-eb44-519f-a803-5a82f181e56f" :answer/type {:db/id #e