id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450107} :answer-field/id #uuid "925d9be4-b3e2-57f7-969e-84df3d94eb40" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d52fcd7c-0cb8-5f3b-83e6-5d87eafb229f" :question/math-academy-id "q-177660" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is a square matrix\n- **II.** $A\\cdot {A}^{T}=I$\n- **III.** $A$ is an orthogonal matrix" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a square matrix $A$ is **orthogonal** if and only if\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}={A}^{T}\\cdot A=I\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the identity matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The number of rows in $A$ is the same as the number of columns. So, it's a square matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\nA\\cdot {A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=I.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${A}^{T}\\cdot A=I,$ our matrix is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133948 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9017b4e-ddb3-56f6-ba30-b494a7e4e09f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Orthogonal Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049606 :topic/id #uuid "03f0df59-343c-5dd7-ad4a-b7bacf1e1f44" :topic/math-academy-id 2105 :topic/title "Orthogonal Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d1a953a-f5cc-5be1-84b3-69be0a7afa05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450108} {:answer/id #uuid "64c1ca58-d0a7-51aa-9436-360d901fce42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64c1ca58-d0a7-51aa-9436-360d901fce42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450109} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bed3038-b384-5d43-92b5-a0801e084f7f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451008} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "387af6f7-f068-535a-b1fa-30498114a5dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450110} {:answer/id #uuid "d52bca8f-a9d5-5566-ae77-cab60157a898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d52bca8f-a9d5-5566-ae77-cab60157a898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450111} :answer-field/id #uuid "969e4688-8a93-5b23-94b5-256f6e748b85" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451009} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82c9c179-5409-5d04-9678-f54cfceb9c1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :a