derate} :question/id #uuid "b608e6a0-7a3f-5af5-a662-35948e07de5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-181279" :question/problem "![](images/08/08754e159a2b204fce6795292c56fb35dd497dc08611ffcbe9d379e1355ab4af.png)\n\nBy finding the missing entries in the schematic shown above for $A\\times B,$ where $A={x,y}$ and $B={0,1,2},$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(x,y)\\in A\\times B$\n- $(x,2)\\in A\\times B$\n- $(1,y)\\in A\\times B$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo complete our schematic of $A\\times B,$ we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of $A$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of $B$ at each intersection.\n\n![](images/c3/c33000e8aa6c217b5607e43e961aaea10586b615d633dc1b59cc598e2f7af56c.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram:\n\n- $(x,y)\\notin A\\times B\\,\\times $\n\n- $(x,2)\\in A\\times B\\,✓$\n\n- $(1,y)\\notin A\\times B\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3de9e532-559c-5fc1-a6ad-5fcd1ed77824" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Special Sets Containing a Given Element" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049887 :topic/id #uuid "1bbcbfec-d0a8-5419-81c9-b34aaaaaa84f" :topic/math-academy-id 47 :topic/title "Special Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c806f15-9ad7-5de9-af21-2047e74fd193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465681} {:answer/id #uuid "c4f4cdb1-adf2-5c6a-9a6a-d1b6e9422d77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465682}] :answer-field/correct {