 $A=\\{a,b,c\\}$ and $B=\\{2,4,6\\},$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\nI. $(4,b)\\in A\\times B$\n\nII. $(c,6)\\in A\\times B$\n\nIII. $(a,2)\\in A\\times B$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo complete our schematic of $A\\times B,$ we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of $A$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of $B$ at each intersection.\n\n![](images/57/57d053cca53046f02201540e655030a37ba8f7a2811e7dc724cf30ca9fd3c072.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram:\n\n- $(4,b)\\notin A\\times B\\,\\times $\n\n- $(c,6)\\in A\\times B\\,✓$\n\n- $(a,2)\\in A\\times B\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287778 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fca5176-1359-5ad8-b012-592ffa9b20b5" :knowledge-point/title "Cartesian Products With Three Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050432 :topic/id #uuid "48930849-af42-52a8-8e89-28eb54e1d4a5" :topic/math-academy-id 49 :topic/title "The Cartesian Product"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ff2d158-b72e-5569-86c7-85fc65a9a7ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465791} {:answer/id #uuid "a3b90b4c-8e62-5aa7-8f8e-cb62a571d3f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3b90b4c-8e62-5aa7-8f8e-cb62a571d3f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465792} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd280a3c-c906-5fe3-8f4c-0d6440e54a52" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466739} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cf618fb-f1d9-5157-869e-44c19617b53b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465793} {:answer/id #uuid "348072d9-0979-5205-ac87-42ed0966ab1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cf618fb-f1d9-5157-869e-44c19617b53b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465793} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d6a0833-9802-5a22-9828-c3db6be203fe" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466740} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ba3e4bf-4d18-5a8a-84a1-20723bf1e792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465795} {:answer/id #uuid "0601d2a9-f68f-5933-b12f-254bdda37ac3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ba3e4bf-4d18-5a8a-84a1-20723bf1e792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465795} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcf6a75b-6257-59f5-b617-d2f9962213bf" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466741}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1ec96a4e-9e05-5335-919b-b747e9d81df8" :question/math-academy-id "q-181969" :question/problem "If $A=\\{p,q,r\\}$ and $B=\\{3,5\\},$ which of the following elements belong to $B\\times (A\\times A)?$\n\nI. $(5,(r,p))$\n\nII. $(q,(5,3))$\n\nIII. $(3,q,p)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times A$ consists of every combination of ${p,q,r}$ with ${p,q,r},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/aa/aad91ef7655fa8a5bf0c9852ee4e5e2166289087a56ac18e932ee3cce17164a0.png)\n\nHence, the set $A\\times A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA\\times A={(p,p),(p,q),(p,r),(q,p),(q,q),(q,r),(r,p),(r,q),(r,r)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times A|=|A|\\cdot |A|=3\\cdot 3=9.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nB\\times (A\\times A)\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $B$ and $A\\times A,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/e5/e573cecaa9333e071d980b1b03d65dafadd027506d2c2b9b6e8acfbe15d3be52.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|B\\times (A\\times A)|=|B|\\cdot |A\\times A|=2\\cdot 9=18.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that only $(5,(r,p))\\in B\\times (A\\times A).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054633 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b304527c-5cdc-57df-b118-e555f6f8fa5c" :knowledge-point/title "Creating a Schematic for a Cartesian Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050432 :topic/id #uuid "48930849-af42-52a8-8e89-28eb54e1d4a5" :topic/math-academy-id 49 :topic/title "The Cartesian Product"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d870ac05-aa32-543b-896b-d5e5e242a31d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465797} {:answer/id #uuid "4cb18d13-5d67-536d-881f-b7a1f61912da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cb18d13-5d67-536d-881f-b7a1f61912da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465798} :answer-field/id #uuid "60c5fad1-a10a-5ff0-8129-22378f8c7c32" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466742} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b95ce0e3-89a4-5a3b-ac08-c99919b8d07b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465799} {:answer/id #uuid "e536a5e9-8e07-5617-acd0-7ac4ae844c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e536a5e9-8e07-5617-acd0-7ac4ae844c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465800} :answer-field/id #uuid "21fec834-65d6-5b83-b9e4-46f7a120a351" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466743} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80d1ae47-c8b9-5fb0-becf-fa45bf191737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465801} {:answer/id #uuid "08565eeb-44f5-5fa8-8e13-13b2a761af2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80d1ae47-c8b9-5fb0-becf-fa45bf191737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465801} :answer-field/id #uuid "1caa5482-3fb1-5560-8b4d-7f2ff4ac7696" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ffb21c72-0872-5ee1-9c14-274c6c7f743e" :question/math-academy-id "q-181975" :question/problem "![](images/bf/bf1c37a92b184cb3e6c81bbd2d653008f5eff0e3b2131f2f297a336881661c22.png)\n\nUsing the visual schematic above for the Cartesian product ${A}^{2}$ for $A={p,q,r},$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(q,q)\\in {A}^{2}$\n- $(p,r)\\in {A}^{2}$\n- ${q}^{2}\\in {A}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The set ${A}^{2}$ is equivalent to the Cartesian product $A\\times A.$\n\nThe Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo complete our schematic of $A\\times A,$ we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of the first set $(A)$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of the second set $(A)$ at each intersection.\n\n![](images/91/919ad6e16dcd1d8f02e8c15c7bd1dfa15f67232c99706dfbc1239e1f9a0f99e5.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram:\n\n- $(q,q)\\in {A}^{2}\\,✓$\n\n- $(p,r)\\in {A}^{2}\\,✓$\n\n- ${q}^{2}\\in {A}^{2}\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fca5176-1359-5ad8-b012-592ffa9b20b5" :knowledge-point/title "Cartesian Products With Three Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050432 :topic/id #uuid "48930849-af42-52a8-8e89-28eb54e1d4a5" :topic/math-academy-id 49 :topic/title "The Cartesian Product"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "158a2d08-6e35-5e32-bd95-015a1d507ed1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465803} {:answer/id #uuid "73c2a068-90a4-5b17-8b65-6668fdc43fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73c2a068-90a4-5b17-8b65-6668fdc43fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465804} :answer-field/id #uuid "705ea8cb-7787-5604-a95c-c0037d9529ea" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466745} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10438c33-6d13-55f8-be0d-81eb594e2ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465805} {:answer/id #uuid "1be3bd42-91e0-5f48-80fa-0782e1cc0500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465806}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1be3bd42-91e0-5f48-80fa-0782e1cc0500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465806} :answer-field/id #uuid "aec6f99e-46fb-5b5f-8258-35d49cd5f8c3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466746} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4ae6b10-3909-58c9-ad25-9c7e2a57005a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465807} {:answer/id #uuid "d0a65fba-63c6-5a3b-b149-ab96fd9f924e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4ae6b10-3909-58c9-ad25-9c7e2a57005a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465807} :answer-field/id #uuid "84eb7871-4c74-53cf-9b44-ffc385343287" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e14f595-c123-5de8-8c3d-4afeb7095ae5" :question/math-academy-id "q-181977" :question/problem "If $A={4,8}$ and $B={x,y,z},$ which of the following elements belong to $A\\times (A\\times B)?$\n- **I.** $(4,(8,z))$\n- **II.** $(8,(8,x))$\n- **III.** $(8,4,y)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${4,8}$ with ${x,y,z},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/72/72feee192b949dcce7b0f10f4e1d772c809bcf73de6c66f15c7de75a4a1ff672.png)\n\nHence, the set $A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(4,x),(4,y),(4,z),(8,x),(8,y),(8,z)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |B|=2\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nA\\times (A\\times B)\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $A$ and $A\\times B,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/1a/1ae41857d4aee82a2a4ad838c20bbe72b05a1505a5f4df3aa4a86fda0fff0612.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times (A\\times B)|=|A|\\cdot |A\\times B|=2\\cdot 6=12.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that both $(4,(8,z))$ and $(8,(8,x))$ are in $A\\times \\text{\\(}A\\times B).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287783 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054633 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b304527c-5cdc-57df-b118-e555f6f8fa5c" :knowledge-point/title "Creating a Schematic for a Cartesian Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050432 :topic/id #uuid "48930849-af42-52a8-8e89-28eb54e1d4a5" :topic/math-academy-id 49 :topic/title "The Cartesian Product"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fae88729-57e9-587a-b6a2-d44889d1457e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465809} {:answer/id #uuid "948516ea-f1bb-5859-b92a-e78c515d269d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fae88729-57e9-587a-b6a2-d44889d1457e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465809} :answer-field/id #uuid "790c0ca6-a144-5485-8ca1-b96ae2004be6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466748} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e43f5d12-98ff-54b4-aaf0-503dce1235fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465811} {:answer/id #uuid "3e637f0a-dbfc-5458-9c1e-c67490980089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e637f0a-dbfc-5458-9c1e-c67490980089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465812} :answer-field/id #uuid "925eab31-abea-5607-92e2-6e84d57f0904" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466749} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76493f21-564c-51be-a712-2569eb913b55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465813} {:answer/id #uuid "66c5a1de-b6e8-5627-a5bf-611191eaa741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66c5a1de-b6e8-5627-a5bf-611191eaa741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465814} :answer-field/id #uuid "abcc1ad3-fdca-5022-9e22-f6c18a6ee080" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16f7d99c-b5b7-5532-9552-dac57833067d" :question/math-academy-id "q-181978" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d6ee87bd861491394c6643679f62cb4b94436bf2777bd2436b3169e779736e2c.png)\n\nUsing the visual schematic above for the Cartesian product ${A}^{2}$ for $A={h,k},$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- ${h}^{2}\\in {A}^{2}$\n- $(h,k)\\in {A}^{2}$\n- $(k,k)\\in {A}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The set ${A}^{2}$ is equivalent to the Cartesian product $A\\times A.$\n\nThe Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo complete our schematic of $A\\times A,$ we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of the first set $(A)$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of the second set $(A)$ at each intersection.\n\n![](images/50/507f8f6306c309d5e894cfb1dabfc2019f371911f7878b196e1f329f1b37dfa6.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram:\n\n- ${h}^{2}\\in {A}^{2}\\,\\times $\n\n- $(h,k)\\in {A}^{2}\\,✓$\n\n- $(k,k)\\in {A}^{2}\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287788 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id 