wer/id #uuid "a43cb5e5-6208-52c0-ba0e-be9cad636149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a43cb5e5-6208-52c0-ba0e-be9cad636149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450125} :answer-field/id #uuid "3462c6d4-91f3-532f-a568-af8fb40ade3e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451016}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "110cd0b0-c05f-5fa3-a734-2910b10ec096" :question/math-academy-id "q-182009" :question/problem "For the sets $A={k,m},$ $B={-1,3,5},$ and $C=A\\times B,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $(-1,k)\\in C$\n- **II.** $(k,m)\\in C$\n- **III.** $(m,3)\\in C$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $A\\times B$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/c6/c660ff6d042bdf228387e5ad55651f02b136f738a2e4fa99c3ef3b3faef3e3c5.png)\n\nHence, the set $C=A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nC={(k,-1),(k,3),(k,5),(m,-1),(m,3),(m,5)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050432 :topic/id #uuid "48930849-af42-52a8-8e89-28eb54e1d4a5" :topic/math-academy-id 49 :topic/title "The Cartesian Product"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f93b4b3-45d3-55bc-83c9-c5f237b38683" :answer/t