ion/math-academy-id "q-182018" :question/problem "For the sets $X={f,g,h}$ and $Z=X\\times X,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $(f,g)\\in Z$\n- **II.** $(f,g,h)\\in Z$\n- **III.** $(h,h)\\in Z$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $X\\times X$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $X.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for ${X}^{2}=X\\times X$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/17/1718bd6f3f2eaa8dd8fe581b0d938b3b5f1928d5e56a11a324f145e7a481fabe.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times X$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(f,f),(f,g),(f,h),(g,f),(g,g),(g,h),(h,f),(h,g),(h,h)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6128eca-7f76-5386-9d67-d81db2943eeb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Cartesian Product" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050432 :topic/id #uuid "48930849-af42-52a8-8e89-28eb54e1d4a5" :topic/math-academy-id 49 :topic/title "The Cartesian Product"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95846851-9e8b-5ceb-9f37-6ad8c04fb4f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465821} {:answer/id #uuid "9afd3716-75a0-5b6c-a94c-e21e54fd24b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465822}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9afd3716-75a0-5b6c-a94c-e21e54fd24b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465822} :answer-field/id #uuid "891afbe7-2139-5274-9bde-c2fc0aa50a55" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466754} {:answer-field/