x} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451040} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b62475b-9e34-5901-b3b2-252278026eb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450174} {:answer/id #uuid "7dbf4583-b589-56d5-8170-cf22b2ea39cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7dbf4583-b589-56d5-8170-cf22b2ea39cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450175} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3621510-26a4-5dc7-bb5c-09395f6b5aac" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1676c625-f838-58d0-a1ed-b9b72fc63c79" :question/math-academy-id "q-20982" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=-{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=-1$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$\n- **II.** $x=0$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$\n- **III.** ${f}^{″}(1)>0$\n- **IV.** $x=1$ is a relative maximum of $f(x)$" :question/worked-solution "We need to identify the critical points. Then, we then need to classify them using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=-{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-4{x}^{3}+4x,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{x}^{3}+4x & =0 \\\\ -4x({x}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ -4x(x-1)(x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,0,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=-1,0,1.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at the critical points. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-12{x}^{2}+4,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-1) & =-8<0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(0) & =4>0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(1) & =-8<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that:\n\n- Statement I is false. The second derivative is negative at $x=-1,$ so this is a relative maximum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statement II is true. The second derivative is positive at $x=0,$ so this is a relative minimum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statement III is false while statement IV is true. The second derivative is negative at $x=1,$ so this is a relative maximum of $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290259 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbee870b-4a67-5ccb-b274-45fac627be6e" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Given Critical Point Using the Second Derivative Test" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048883 :topic/id #uuid "c96abbae-0759-5f81-9064-a4b37d0b7422" :topic/math-academy-id 339 :topic/title "The Second Derivative Test"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28647c8d-4e8f-57ff-b684-32be4e568f93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465827} {:answer/id #uuid "34c6fe0b-a8ad-5fd9-aeb4-86f2e50df8aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34c6fe0b-a8ad-5fd9-aeb4-86f2e50df8aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465828} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f1146a9-10ee-58b8-94c8-f3a680255e30" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466757} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "268ffdcd-667c-544c-bc23-360a262c796a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465829} {:answer/id #uuid "c559cc34-97ab-5326-abee-590301d3ea53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "268ffdcd-667c-544c-bc23-360a262c796a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465829} :answer-field/id #uuid "64d9dcfc-ac33-5ace-8683-bacd9076f2a3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466758} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24f8b749-3169-5d99-b3ab-2b4f4afd0b8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465831} {:answer/id #uuid "489ce9b4-9556-5322-bdad-c68e6b5f09be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24f8b749-3169-5d99-b3ab-2b4f4afd0b8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465831} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1ef321f-b386-5632-8cec-c42e20b7fd95" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466759}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "206675d2-b06e-5deb-b30d-ae541d334107" :question/math-academy-id "q-20983" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+24x.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(2)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${f}^{″}(2)=0$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=2$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=2$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We're given that $x=2$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+24x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=6{x}^{2}-24x+24.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=12x-24.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(2) & =12\\cdot 2-24=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is zero, we conclude that the test is inconclusive, we need to use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's  find other stationary points. These points are the solution of the equation ${f}^{′}(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-24x+24 & =0 \\\\ 6(x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the only stationary point is $x=2.$\n\nLet's choose auxiliary points from each side of the stationary point and evaluate the first derivative at them. We take the auxiliary points $x=1,3$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =6(1)^{2}-24(1)+24=6>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =6(3)^{2}-24(3)+24=6>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the first derivative does not change the sign at $x=2$, we conclude that $f(x)$ has no relative extrema at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Coordinates of an Image Formed by a Singular Transformation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049254 :topic/id #uuid "e6f9ad03-abe7-52d6-8a6a-acbcb8fbeef7" :topic/math-academy-id 1351 :topic/title "Singular Linear Transformations in the Plane"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b7e659d-56db-586b-9e30-c199a47f2d57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465833} {:answer/id #uuid "41838cf6-58b8-5e7b-91fe-8ddaa9cdf51f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41838cf6-58b8-5e7b-91fe-8ddaa9cdf51f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465834} :answer-field/id #uuid "eeed986f-a33a-5850-af4c-a59b7f254892" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de977d43-0252-5c01-a917-431cef599417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465835} {:answer/id #uuid "8d16f839-433d-5708-912f-a65fbd85a727" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d16f839-433d-5708-912f-a65fbd85a727" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465836} :answer-field/id #uuid "201f9d6e-4534-5596-90d4-245690e6ae7a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466761} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b244ad2c-e740-5756-9eb8-97804bc79c63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465837} {:answer/id #uuid "d91709c7-2d43-578b-891b-0b8c42602c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b244ad2c-e740-5756-9eb8-97804bc79c63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465837} :answer-field/id #uuid "aee47c52-cc29-52cc-886a-27d07b5a1c28" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b1e5b57c-3102-59cd-a153-f7966b8c71f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-21066" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,2)$, $(-1,1)$ and $(3,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(12,6)$\n- **II.** $(4,2)$\n- **III.** $(4,6)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 4 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(12,6)$, $(4,2)$ and $(12,6).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290273 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Coordinates of an Image Formed by a Singular Transformation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049254 :topic/id #uuid "e6f9ad03-abe7-52d6-8a6a-acbcb8fbeef7" :topic/math-academy-id 1351 :topic/title "Singular Linear Transformations in the Plane"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id 